.SS "\fBclient_funs\fP* noir_sess_client_get (\fBnoir_sess\fP * ns, const char * tag)"
.PP
get the view object for a certain view in a given session 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
the view-object, or NULL 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIns\fP the session/window 
.br
\fItag\fP the name/tag of the view
.RE
.PP

.SS "void* noir_sess_client_get_data (\fBnoir_sess\fP * ns, const char * tag)"
.PP
get user-data from the view-object for a certain view in a given session. 
.PP
the user-data usually hold administrative struct (browser_view *, icon_view *, ...). 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
the user-data, or NULL 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIns\fP the session/window 
.br
\fItag\fP the name/tag of the view
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBclient_funs\fP* noir_sess_client_lock (long serial, const char * tag)"
.PP
get a view object and lock it. 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
a view-object, or NULL 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIserial\fP the serial number of the session to acquire 
.br
\fItag\fP the name of the view
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBclient_funs\fP* noir_sess_client_register (\fBnoir_sess\fP * ns, const char * name, void * data)"
.PP
register a view with both the session and the model. 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
the new view object, or NULL 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIns\fP the session to register in (will become part of ns->clients chain) 
.br
\fIname\fP the name-tag for the view 
.br
\fIdata\fP user-data (usually administrative struct, browser_view *, icon_view *, ...)
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBclient_funs\fP* noir_sess_client_register_full (\fBnoir_sess\fP * ns, const char * name, void * data, int(*)(\fBfile_info\fP *, \fBmodel_event\fP type, \fBfile_flags\fP changed, void *) evt_view, int(*)(void **) dst_data, int(*)(void *) set_selection)"
.PP
register a view with both the session and the model and set callbacks. 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
the new view object, or NULL 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIns\fP the session to register in (will become part of ns->clients chain) 
.br
\fIname\fP the name-tag for the view 
.br
\fIdata\fP user-data (usually administrative struct, browser_view *, icon_view *, ...) 
.br
\fIevt_view\fP what to call when the contents of the model change (new file, ...) 
.br
\fIdst_data\fP when this entry is destroyed, call this function to release user-data 
.br
\fIset_selection\fP what to call to set ns->selection on the view
.RE
.PP

.SS "void noir_sess_client_unlock (\fBclient_funs\fP * c)"
.PP
release a lock on a view object 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIc\fP the view-object
.RE
.PP

.SS "int noir_sess_client_unregister (\fBnoir_sess\fP * ns, \fBclient_funs\fP * cf)"
.PP
remove a view from a session. 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
NOIR_SUCC (done), NOIR_FAIL (einval), NOIR_NOTFOUND (unknown view) 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIns\fP the session to remove the view from 
.br
\fIcf\fP the view-object
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBnoir_sess\fP* noir_sess_copy (\fBnoir_sess\fP * d, \fBnoir_sess\fP * s)"
.PP
copy session struct 's' to struct 'd', a proto-struct obtained with \fBnoir_sess_new()\fP. 
.PP
'd' will retain the serial issued by \fBnoir_sess_new()\fP rather than duplicate that of 's'. 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
the new session 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fId\fP buffer for the destination-session 
.br
\fIs\fP the source-session
.RE
.PP

.SS "int noir_sess_drop (\fBnoir_sess\fP * ns)"
.PP
drop the session associated with a window. 
.PP
hook this into the 'window-destroyed' callback of your toolkit.
.PP
lock the session-chain's lock, find the session, remove it from the chain, then call \fBnoir_sess_free()\fP on it. unlock.
.PP
called from \fBevidence::closed()\fP. 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
an error-code 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIns\fP the session to drop
.RE
.PP

.SS "static void noir_sess_free (\fBnoir_sess\fP * ns)\fC [static]\fP"
.PP
free memory associated with a session. 
.PP
session is expected to already have been removed from session-list. if the session still has views ('clients'), these will be removed. called from \fBnoir_sess_drop()\fP. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIns\fP the session to remove
.RE
.PP

